    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11581" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπάρχω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ξω</span> (v. infr.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lead the way,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς νᾶσον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					11.6
				</span></i>
			 (s. v.l.); esp. in dancing, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ
				ἀπάρχων τῶν ὀρχηστῶν</span> dub. l. in <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				7.73
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὔμμι δ᾽ ἀπάρξει</span>
			<i>shall lead</i> you <i>in the dance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				9.189
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> prob.
				<i>reign far away</i> from home, of Teucer, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				4.46
			</span></i>.</div>
